# Pasankalla mobile-router defaults. Managed by /usr/sbin/pasankalla.
config pasankalla 'settings'
	# Master switch for the guest AP, travelmate and the status LEDs.
	# When 0 the guest BSSes are disabled, travelmate is stopped and both
	# LEDs are turned off.
	option enabled '1'

	# Guest AP. The SSID is used verbatim; new sections are created with
	# encryption 'owe' (no transition/open twin). Existing AP sections on
	# this SSID and on guest_network are adopted as-is, which keeps the
	# original Pasankalla open+hidden-OWE transition pair working.
	option guest_ssid 'Pasankalla gratis'
	option guest_network 'lanclientes'

	# When travelmate uses the same radio as a 5 GHz guest BSS, disable
	# that BSS (the old Pasankalla scripts did this to avoid AP+STA
	# scanning on the same weak radio). Set to 0 to keep it up.
	option guest_5g_follow_uplink '1'

	# Slider logical state: gpio-button-hotplug reports pressed/released
	# for BTN_0 at boot and on every flip. Set to 1 if the slider is wired
	# the other way round on a board revision.
	option slider_invert '0'

	# At boot, wait this many seconds for the ethernet WAN to obtain its
	# DHCP lease before starting travelmate. Without it a fast boot would
	# briefly start a 5 GHz scan on a router whose WAN is actually connected.
	# 0 disables the wait.
	option wan_grace '20'

	# Seconds without a WAN or travelmate lease before the "no internet"
	# state (white off, red slow blink) is shown. Travelmate keeps
	# searching during and after this grace period.
	option offline_after '60'

	# Poll period. Button/interface/wireless hotplug events apply the state
	# immediately, but swconfig targets (mt7628) never raise notification
	# for a dead switch port, so the wired-WAN check below has to run on
	# the poll. An apply forks uci/ifstatus/jsonfilter/swconfig a few dozen
	# times (~2 s on the TR1200 when the router is otherwise busy), so the
	# poll only starts a new apply once the previous one has finished.
	option poll_interval '10'

	# How long the WAN port may stay without carrier before the WAN counts
	# as down even though netifd still reports a lease (swconfig keeps
	# eth0.2 "up" after the cable is pulled). Debounces cable/port
	# renegotiation. 0 disables the check.
	option wan_down_after '30'

	# How often to look for travelmate while it is the uplink and has no
	# lease (seconds). Restarting it makes wpa_supplicant scan again; every
	# restart flaps its STA, so this must stay well above one scan. 0 disables.
	option travelmate_retry '120'

	# sysfs LED names (both boards expose these labels from their DTS).
	option led_white 'white:status'
	option led_red 'red:power'

	# Internal one-shot marker: zz-pasankalla sets this to 1 after pointing
	# antilag at the WAN netdev and enabling it. Do not set it by hand.
	# (Tailscale used to be disabled here too; it is no longer touched.)
	option defaults_version '0'

	# Managed by zz-pasankalla: wifi-iface section names that belong to the
	# guest AP. Empty means "discover by guest_ssid + guest_network".
	# list guest_sections 'pasankalla2'
	# list guest_sections 'pasankalla5'
